EXT. SKI GONDOLA CABIN - DUSK

A steel and glass cabin hangs motionless over a snowy chasm, tilting slightly in the wind. Pines far below. A cable creaks. Five people crowd the benches, breath fogging the windows.

CALLUM DRAKE (50s, patrol jacket) stands by the door. BRIGID HENNESSY-ABE (30s, snowboarder, goggles on forehead) kneels on the floor. SANTIAGO OYELOWO (40s, hotelier, fur-lined coat) sits, hands folded. MAGDALENA VOSS (60s, hiker, thermos on her knee) sips tea. EMERSON LAROCHE (20s, student, backpack on his lap) stares at the dark.

                    CALLUM
          Rescue knows we're here. They said three hours.

                    BRIGID
          It's been four.

                    CALLUM
          They said three to start.

                    SANTIAGO
          And when do they finish?

                    CALLUM
          When they finish.

                    MAGDALENA
          Tea?

                    EMERSON
          Please.

                    MAGDALENA
          One cup. We share.

                    BRIGID
          I'm not drinking from a stranger's thermos.

                    MAGDALENA
          I'm Magdalena. Now I'm not a stranger.

                    BRIGID
          Brigid.

                    MAGDALENA
          Brigid. Drink.

                    SANTIAGO
          The wind is picking up.

                    CALLUM
          It does that.

                    SANTIAGO
          It rocks the cabin.

                    CALLUM
          It's rated for ninety miles an hour.

                    EMERSON
          What's the wind now?

                    CALLUM
          Thirty.

                    BRIGID
          And the temperature?

                    CALLUM
          Minus eight.

                    MAGDALENA
          Minus eight with wind chill is minus fifteen, dear.

                    CALLUM
          Fine.

                    SANTIAGO
          How long before cold becomes dangerous?

                    CALLUM
          For five people in a closed cabin? Hours.

                    EMERSON
          How many hours?

                    CALLUM
          More than we need.

                    BRIGID
          You're lying.

                    CALLUM
          I'm managing expectations.

                    MAGDALENA
          He's doing what he can.

                    BRIGID
          Who?

                    MAGDALENA
          The patrolman.

                    BRIGID
          She meant Callum. Say Callum.

                    MAGDALENA
          I said "he."

                    BRIGID
          I know. It's unclear. He, he, he.

                    EMERSON
          Can we not?

                    SANTIAGO
          She's right though. We have two men, two women, and a kid.

                    EMERSON
          I'm twenty-two.

                    SANTIAGO
          And a very tall kid.

                    CALLUM
          Everyone, listen. We stay calm, we stay warm, we stay together.

                    BRIGID
          And if the cable snaps?

                    CALLUM
          It won't.

                    BRIGID
          If it does?

                    CALLUM
          Then we hold hands.

Nobody laughs. Nobody speaks. The cabin sways, creaks, settles. A snowflake lands on the glass and melts into a perfect bead.
